        "tipo": "intro",
        "min": 3,
        "texto": "Listen first, read later. Next to every letter, word and sentence there is a speaker: tap it, listen and repeat out loud. German is written the way it is spoken, and the pronunciation rules are few and regular. In this lesson you hear and read German for the first time: you learn the sounds, read new words without fear and finish with your first greetings. In the tables, «ç» marks the soft sound of «ch» (like the «h» in «hue») and «kh» marks the harsh sound (like the «ch» in Scottish «loch»)."
